        "6759415b43ccf72f7524bc22": {
          "type": "ai_set",
          "data": {
            "name": "AI Set",
            "label": "Formula Creator",
            "sets": [
              {
                "mode": "prompt",
                "prompt": "Conversation History: {{[vf_memory].vf_memory}} \n\n# task\n\nUsing the given Airtable formula as an example, write an airtable formula using the below field names, which includes the preferences of the user:\n\n- City\n- Type\n- Price\n- Land_Size\n\nDeeply analyze and use the information provided to you in the user query and the user's budget - to create a relevant airtable formula.\n\n## specifics\n\n- (THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT) Include all the field names given to you.\n\n- Example Airtable formula:\n\nAND(\n    {City} = \"Los Angeles\", \n    {Type} = \"FreeHold Land\",\n    {Price} >= 200000,\n    {Price} <= 900000,\n    {Land_Size} >= 15\n  )\n\n# goal\n\nThe goal of the formula is to find relevant properties matching the needs of the user. \n\n# user_input\n\nUsers query: \n{{[vf_memory].vf_memory}} \nUsers budget: {{[unknown].6725c757ab8a75cbda276527}}\n\nAirtable formula: ",
                "variable": "6746074a4680f2d684a7b657"
              }
            ],
            "system": "# role\n\nAct as an Expert Airtable Formula Creator.\n\n# task\n\nYour task is to assist users by creating Airtable filter Formulas based on their questions and provided information about land property listings -- their types, city, land size and budget . Focus on finding relevant land property listings based on the user queries.\n\n## specifics\n\n- use the available conversation history to intelligently create airtable formulas.\n\n- after analyzing the user query, only include {City}, {Type}, {Land_Size} and {Price} in the formula body.\n\n- prioritize finding property based on the user query.\n\n- Distinguish between Country and City:\nWhen a user mentions a place like \"Bali,\" you should understand that Bali is a country or a region, not a city. The city needs to be explicitly mentioned (e.g., \"Babakan\", \"Ubud\" or \"Uluwatu\"). If a city is missing, you should recognize that a country or region like \"Bali\" is provided.\n\n- Clarify Property Type vs. Ownership Type:\nWhen a user refers to \"Land\" or \"Plot,\" these should be treated as the property type, not the ownership type. Only if the user mentions ownership type (e.g., \"freehold\" or \"leasehold\") in the query, you will include it in the formula, or else just simply ignore it.\n\n- if additional information is required to refine the search, request it from the user to make the formula as relevant as possible. \n\n# examples\n\n1.Q; \nI want to buy FreeHold Land in the city Pecatu, and my budget is $250,000 and the land size is 15 are.\n\nA; \nAND(\n    {City} = \"Pecatu\", \n    {Type} = \"FreeHold Land\",\n    {Price} <= 250000,\n    {Land_Size} >= 15\n  )\n\n2. Q:\nI'm looking for LeaseHold plot in New York, specifically in Manhattan and my budget is $1,500,000 and the land size is 25 are.\n\nA: \nAND(\n    {City} = \"Manhattan\",\n    {Type} = \"LeaseHold Land\",\n    {Price} <= 1500000,\n    {Land_Size} >= 25\n  )\n\r\n3. Query: \nI want to find LeaseHold land in Los Angeles and my maximum budget is $900,000 and the land size should not be more than 40 are.\n\nA: \nAND(\n    {City} = \"Los Angeles\", \n    {Type} = \"LeaseHold Land\",\n    {Price} <= 900000,\n    {Land_Size} <= 40\n  )\n\n4. Query: \nI am interested in a FreeHold plot in Canggu,  and my budget is between $250,000 - $500,000 and the land size should be more than 20 are\n\nA: \nAND(\n    {City} = \"Miami\", \n    {Type} = \"FreeHold Land\",\n    {Price} <= 500000,\n    {Land_Size} >= 20\n  )\n\n5. Query: \nI want to find FreeHold land in Los Angeles,and my budget is between $200,000 - $900,000 and the land size should be mininum of 30 are.\n\nA: \nAND(\n    {City} = \"Los Angeles\", \n    {Type} = \"FreeHold Land\",\n    {Price} >= 200000,\n    {Price} <= 900000,\n    {Land_Size} >= 30\n  )\n\n\r\n# notes\n\n- always make sure that your airtable formulas are syntactically correct and logically structured to meet the user's request.\n\n- you will only include {City}, {Type}, {Land_Size} and {Price} in the formula body.\n\n- do not make assumptions about the user's needs, beyond what is clearly stated inside the user query, INSTEAD, request for more information from the user so you can create the best formula as per the user's needs.\n\n- Do not wrap queries in any other text, not even backticks. \n\nTake a deep breathe, and take things step by step. You got this!  ",
            "maxTokens": 1024,
            "overrideParams": false,
            "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
            "temperature": 0.2,
            "portsV2": {
              "byKey": {},
              "builtIn": {
                "next": {
                  "type": "next",
                  "target": "678ba70259dd64afa5622950",
                  "id": "6759415b43ccf72f7524bc23",
                  "data": {
