        "67598ddf43ccf72f75253bf0": {
          "type": "ai_set",
          "data": {
            "name": "AI Set",
            "label": "Set Size field",
            "sets": [
              {
                "mode": "prompt",
                "prompt": "Conversation history:\n{{[vf_memory].vf_memory}}",
                "variable": "67309bb49f1273d401e3dbd4"
              }
            ],
            "system": "# Role \n\nyou are an expert Chat Transcript Analyst.\n\n# task \n\nAnalyze the chat conversation history and find the size of a land mentioned by the user for buying land. \n\n## specifics\n\n- Only output the number of the size of the land, do not output the area units.\n\n# examples\n\n1.\nQ:  Conversation history: assistant: Let me collect some information first, this way I can find the best properties, matching your needs.In which city/area are you looking to buy Land?user: i wanna buy a 100m2 landassistant: Let me collect some information first, this way I can find the best properties, matching your needs.In which city/area are you looking to buy Land?user: Cangguassistant: That's a great step.How would you like to own the Land?user: FreeHold Land\n\nA: 100\n\n2. Q:  Conversation history: assistant: Let me collect some information first, this way I can find the best properties, matching your needs.In which city/area are you looking to buy Land?user: i wanna buy a 15 are landassistant: Let me collect some information first, this way I can find the best properties, matching your needs.In which city/area are you looking to buy Land?user: Cangguassistant: That's a great step.How would you like to own the Land?user: FreeHold Land\n\nA: 15\n\n# output\n\n- You will only output the area of land mentioned in the conversation history. \n- (THIS IS A VERY IMPORTANT STEP) your output should only contain the area of land mentioned by the user.\n- Do not explain your answers.\n- Do not wrap your answers in any other text, not even backticks.",
            "maxTokens": 1024,
            "overrideParams": false,
            "model": "claude-3.5-haiku",
            "temperature": 0.2,
