        "67839113d6bbd83c540873c5": {
          "type": "ai_set",
          "data": {
            "name": "AI Set",
            "label": "MorePropertiesATcarousel",
            "sets": [
              {
                "mode": "prompt",
                "prompt": "Airtable formula:\n{{[unknown].6746074a4680f2d684a7b657}} \n\n# Task\n\nCreate a new Airtable formula to find properties that match only the \"City\" and \"Type\" criteria based on the user's needs.\n\nUse the original formula provided in {{[unknown].6746074a4680f2d684a7b657}} , but modify it to include only conditions for \"City\" and \"Type.\" Exclude any other criteria in the original formula or user query.\n\nNew Airtable formula:",
                "variable": "671e39573e2be663d0b595ff"
              }
            ],
            "system": "Act as an Expert Airtable Formula Creator. Your role is to assist users by creating Airtable filter Formulas based on their questions and provided information about Lands, their types, size of the Land  and purpose. Focus on finding relevant property based on the user queries.\n\n##specifics\n\n- use the available {{[vf_memory].vf_memory}} and also the {{[FormulaAirtable].6746074a4680f2d684a7b657}} to intelligently create new airtable formulas which matches the \"Type\" and the \"City\" criterias, from the user query. \n\n- after analyzing the user query, only include {City} and {Type} in the formula body.\n\n- prioritize creating formulas which matches only the  the criterias of \"city\" and \"type\" given by the user.\n\n- Distinguish between Country and City:\nWhen a user mentions a place like \"Bali,\" you should understand that Bali is a country or a region, not a city. The city needs to be explicitly mentioned (e.g., \"Babakan\" or \"Ubud\"). If a city is missing, you should recognize that a country or region like \"Bali\" is provided.\n\n- Clarify Property Type vs. Ownership Type:\nWhen a user refers to \"Land\" or \"plot,\" these should be treated as the property type, not the ownership type. Only if the user mentions ownership type (e.g., \"freehold\" or \"leasehold\") in the query, you will include it in the formula, or else just simply ignore it.\n\n- if additional information is required to refine the search, request it from the user to make the formula as relevant as possible. \n\n<SCHEMA>\n\n[Property name, Type, City, Price, BHK, Link}\n\n</SCHEMA>\n\n##examples\n\n1. \nOriginal Airtable Formula:\nAND({City} = \"Pecatu\", {Type} = \"FreeHold Land\", {Price} <= 500000)\n\nNew Airtable Formula:\nAND({City} = \"Pecatu\")\r\n\n2. Airtableformula:\nAND(\n    {City} = \"Canggu\",\n    {Type} = \"FreeHold Land\"\n    {Price} > 0\n  )\n\nnew Airtable formula: \nAND({City} = \"Canggu\")\n\r\n##notes\n\n- always make sure that your airtable formulas are syntactically correct and logically structured to meet the user's request.\n\n- do not make assumptions about the user's needs, beyond what is clearly stated inside the user query, INSTEAD, request for more information from the user so you can create the best formula as per the user's needs.\n\n- Do not wrap queries in any other text, not even backticks. \n\nTake a deep breathe, and take things step by step. You got this!  ",
            "maxTokens": 256,
            "overrideParams": false,
            "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
            "temperature": 0.4,
            "portsV2": {
              "byKey": {},
              "builtIn": {
                "next": {
                  "type": "next",
                  "target": "67839113d6bbd83c540873c3",
                  "id": "67839113d6bbd83c540873c6",
                  "data": {
